From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: emuTOS-MCD <darekadumon@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 05:50:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 099/190] segacd: the diagnostic is the default; a direction is
 the way out

Which button registers at power-on has now cost two hardware runs.
Left never fired at all. The only log this port has came off Up, which
selected an image on a four-era disc where the diagnostic was compiled
in unconditionally -- on this build Up is cd_selftest, a different
lever entirely. Asking for a specific button on a disc whose only
purpose is to run the diagnostic is a coin flip that has already
landed wrong twice.

So holding nothing runs it, and any of Left, Up or Right skips to the
desktop. The escape no longer rests on one button working.

Set at the flag decode rather than at the test in biosmain, and that
distinction turned out to matter. The first version was an || at the
use site, and it read the disc with a different driver: segacd_diag
also sets cd_ts_want, so a default run went through our own CD code
while a Down run went through the parked firmware. Under gpgx the
difference was visible immediately -- the default run's Fread returned
32 bytes and reported success, and every one of them was
non-printable, where the Down run returned the file. Two runs of the
same disc that could not be compared, which is the opposite of what
this image is for. Setting the flag makes them one run.

Both now read `Fread 32 [This file is on the comp]` under gpgx and
differ only in the button word they print.
